L001128	\section{Instrument assemblage and channel steering under amplitude damping channel and noisy Pauli measurements}\label{appendix: instrument assemblage}
L001129	
L001130	Here, as a concrete example, we consider the total channel $\Lambda^{C \to B} \to \Lambda^{\rm amp}_{\gamma}$ to be a qubit-amplitude-damping channel with Kraus operators
L001131	\begin{equation}
L001132	    K_{0} =
L001133	    \left(\begin{matrix}
L001134	        1 & 0 \\
L001135	        0 & \sqrt{1-\gamma}
L001136	    \end{matrix}\right)\quad\text{and}\quad
L001137	    K_{1}=
L001138	    \left(\begin{matrix}
L001139	        0 & \sqrt{\gamma} \\
L001140	        0 & 0
L001141	    \end{matrix}\right)\quad \text{with} \quad \gamma \in [0,1].
L001142	\end{equation}
L001143	In such a case, the minimal dilation can be found as
L001144	\begin{equation}
L001145	    V_\gamma \ket{\psi}= \sum_{i=0}^1 \ket{i}\otimes K_{i} \ket{\psi}.
L001146	\end{equation}
L001147	As we consider the input state $\rho^{\rm C} \to \ket{1}\bra{1}$, the extended channel $\Lambda^{C \to A \otimes B}$ can be written as
L001148	\begin{equation}
L001149	\begin{aligned}
L001150	    \Lambda^{C \to A \otimes B}\left(\ket{1}\bra{1}\right)
L001151	    &= V_\gamma \ket{1}\bra{1} V_\gamma^\dagger \\
L001152	    &= \sum_{i,j} \sqrt{\alpha_i \alpha_j}\,\ket{i}\bra{j}\otimes\ket{i\oplus1}\bra{j\oplus1},
L001153	\end{aligned}
L001154	\end{equation}
L001155	where $\alpha_0 = 1-\gamma$ and $\alpha_1 = \gamma$.
L001156	The output state from the extend channel is pure entangled, and  $\alpha_i$ represent the Schmidt coefficients.
L001157	For $\gamma \in \{0,1\}$, the output state is separable, and thus, indicating the impossibility for Alice to steer Bob's outputs of the channel.
L001158	
L001159	
L001160	Together with two noisy qubit Pauli measurements and inpute state $\ket{1}$, we can set the instrument assemblage as
L001161	\begin{equation}
L001162	\begin{aligned}
L001163	     \Lambda_{\gamma, a|x}^w (\ket{1}\bra{1})
L001164	     &= \Tr_{\rm A} \, (M^w_{a|x}\otimes \id ) V_\gamma \ket{1}\bra{1} V_\gamma^\dagger \\
L001165	     &= \Tr_{\rm A} \, (M^w_{a|x}\otimes \id ) \sum_{i,j} \ket{i}\bra{j}\otimes K_i \, \ket{1}\bra{1}\, K_j^{\dagger} \\
L001166	     &= \sum_{i,j} \bra{j}M_{a|x}^{w}\ket{i} \sqrt{\alpha_i \alpha_j}\ket{i\oplus1}\bra{j\oplus1},
L001167	\end{aligned}
L001168	\end{equation}
L001169	which satisfies $\sum_{a} \Lambda_{\gamma, a|x}^w = \Lambda^{\rm amp}_{\gamma}~~\forall x,w$.
L001170	We note that for $\gamma = 0.5$, $V_{\gamma = 0.5}$ directly maps $\ket{1}$ to a maximally entangled state, and consequently reproduces the result of the incompatible measurement assemblage as shown in Appendix.~\ref{appendix: measurement assemblage example}.
L001171	
